# Authentication and Authorization

- Use Better Auth as the only auth system. Follow the official MongoDB adapter and Express guides.
- Import `mongodbAdapter` from `@better-auth/mongo-adapter` and pass a native `MongoClient` database. Pass `client` when the deployment supports transactions.
- Mount `toNodeHandler(auth)` before `express.json()`. This project uses Express 5 and mounts `/api/auth/*splat`.
- Load the session with `auth.api.getSession({ headers: fromNodeHeaders(req.headers) })`.
- Store `role` with Better Auth `additionalFields` and `input: false`. Allowed values: `admin`, `manager`, `waiter`, `chef`, `cashier`, `customer`. Default `customer`.
- Keep client route groups aligned with the six roles in this rule. This server role list is the authorization source of truth; do not add another role list.
- Ignore `role`, `isAdmin`, or permission flags from the body, query, or custom headers.

```javascript
export function requireRole(...roles) {
  return (req, res, next) => {
    if (!req.user) return next(new AppError("Unauthorized", 401));
    if (!roles.includes(req.user.role)) return next(new AppError("Forbidden", 403));
    next();
  };
}
```

## Who can do what

- `admin`: full access
- `manager`: menu, tables, reservations, inventory, coupons, reports, refunds
- `waiter`: tables, orders, reservations
- `chef`: kitchen status `preparing` and `ready`, inventory read
- `cashier`: bills, payments, completing an order
- `customer`: own orders, reservations, and reviews

Every mutation checks the session on the server. Customers may read and change only their own records.
